



Version 3. Corrected. The changes are: total tilePower on TILE (no index-out-of-domain), TriageFn and Infer as CONSTANTS (implementation-supplied, not invented operators), proper vars/Spec/WF_vars, no primed variables in invariants, no stub invariants, and every claim stated at the scope the artifact actually establishes.

Three files.

File 1 — STT1024.tla (the standard's formal core)

```tla
--------------------------- MODULE STT1024 ---------------------------
(***********************************************************************)
(* ST-T1024 — Formal Core (v3.0)                                       *)
(* License: Apache-2.0                                                 *)
(*                                                                     *)
(* Register:                                                           *)
(*   SHALL  — requirement on a conforming implementation              *)
(*   SHOULD — recommendation                                           *)
(*   MAY    — optional                                                 *)
(*                                                                     *)
(* In scope:  the scheduler FSM, the cycle budget as a REQUIREMENT,    *)
(*            tile isolation, the timeout safety net.                  *)
(*                                                                     *)
(* Out of scope:  TriageFn and Infer internals, power-gating physics,  *)
(*                SK-1024 (separate module), tile count (parameter),   *)
(*                determinism (conformance requirement, not a state    *)
(*                invariant — see §5 of the standard text).            *)
(***********************************************************************)

EXTENDS Integers, Sequences, FiniteSets

CONSTANTS
    Tiles,        \* SHALL be a non-empty set of tile identifiers
    Inputs,       \* SHALL be a non-empty set of admissible normalized queries
    TriageFn,     \* SHALL be a pure function Inputs -> (Tiles \cup {0})
    Infer,        \* SHALL be a pure function (Tiles \X Inputs) -> STRING
    MaxCycles,    \* SHALL be a positive integer
    MaxQueryLen,  \* SHALL be a positive integer
    MaxHistory    \* SHALL be a positive integer

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Cycle budget.  These are REQUIREMENTS, not derivations.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
C_HARVEST   == 0
C_TRIAGE    == 10
C_SCHEDULE  == 5
C_ACTIVATE  == 1
C_EXECUTE   == 380
C_POWERDOWN == 1
C_TOTAL     == C_HARVEST + C_TRIAGE + C_SCHEDULE + C_ACTIVATE
             + C_EXECUTE + C_POWERDOWN

ASSUME Tiles # {}
ASSUME Inputs # {}
ASSUME MaxCycles \in Nat /\ MaxCycles > 0
ASSUME MaxQueryLen \in Nat /\ MaxQueryLen > 0
ASSUME MaxHistory \in Nat /\ MaxHistory > 0
ASSUME C_TOTAL <= MaxCycles
ASSUME \A q \in Inputs : Len(q) <= MaxQueryLen

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Types
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
TILE    == Tiles \cup {0}
POWER   == {"ON", "OFF"}
STATES  == {"IDLE", "HARVEST", "TRIAGE", "SCHEDULE", "EXECUTE", "POWERDOWN"}
LABELS  == {"HARVEST", "TRIAGE", "SCHEDULE", "ACTIVATE",
            "EXECUTE", "POWERDOWN", "TIMEOUT"}
Histories == UNION { [1..n -> LABELS] : n \in 0..MaxHistory }
Results   == {""} \cup { Infer[t, q] : t \in Tiles, q \in Inputs }

VARIABLES
    state, activeTile, cycleCounter, query, result, errorCode,
    tilePower, history

vars == <<state, activeTile, cycleCounter, query, result,
          errorCode, tilePower, history>>

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
AllOff == [t \in TILE |-> "OFF"]

AppendBounded(h, x) ==
    IF Len(h) < MaxHistory
    THEN Append(h, x)
    ELSE Append(Tail(h), x)

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Type invariant (SHALL)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
TypeOK ==
    /\ state \in STATES
    /\ activeTile \in TILE
    /\ cycleCounter \in 0..MaxCycles
    /\ query \in Inputs \cup {""}
    /\ result \in Results
    /\ errorCode \in {"", "0x-AMBIG", "0x-TIMEOUT"}
    /\ tilePower \in [TILE -> POWER]
    /\ tilePower[0] = "OFF"
    /\ history \in Histories

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Initial state
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Init ==
    /\ state = "IDLE"
    /\ activeTile = 0
    /\ cycleCounter = 0
    /\ query = ""
    /\ result = ""
    /\ errorCode = ""
    /\ tilePower = AllOff
    /\ history = <<>>

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actions
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

\* Stage 1.  Acquire a query.  Resets the per-query cycle counter.
HarvestIntent ==
    /\ state = "IDLE"
    /\ \E q \in Inputs : query' = q
    /\ state' = "HARVEST"
    /\ cycleCounter' = C_HARVEST
    /\ errorCode' = ""
    /\ history' = AppendBounded(history, "HARVEST")
    /\ UNCHANGED <<activeTile, result, tilePower>>

\* Stage 2.  Deterministic triage.  Tile 0 means ambiguity.
FISTriage ==
    /\ state = "HARVEST"
    /\ LET t == TriageFn[query] IN
       /\ activeTile' = t
       /\ IF t = 0
          THEN /\ state' = "IDLE"
               /\ errorCode' = "0x-AMBIG"
          ELSE /\ state' = "TRIAGE"
               /\ errorCode' = ""
    /\ cycleCounter' = cycleCounter + C_TRIAGE
    /\ history' = AppendBounded(history, "TRIAGE")
    /\ UNCHANGED <<query, result, tilePower>>

\* Stage 3.  Schedule.
FSMSchedule ==
    /\ state = "TRIAGE"
    /\ activeTile /= 0
    /\ state' = "SCHEDULE"
    /\ cycleCounter' = cycleCounter + C_SCHEDULE
    /\ history' = AppendBounded(history, "SCHEDULE")
    /\ UNCHANGED <<activeTile, query, result, errorCode, tilePower>>

\* Stage 4.  Power exactly one tile.  Resets all others to OFF.
TileActivation ==
    /\ state = "SCHEDULE"
    /\ activeTile /= 0
    /\ tilePower' = [t \in TILE |-> IF t = activeTile THEN "ON" ELSE "OFF"]
    /\ state' = "EXECUTE"
    /\ cycleCounter' = cycleCounter + C_ACTIVATE
    /\ history' = AppendBounded(history, "ACTIVATE")
    /\ UNCHANGED <<activeTile, query, result, errorCode>>

\* Stage 5.  Deterministic inference.  Infer is supplied by the
\* implementation.  The standard requires purity, not a definition.
Execute ==
    /\ state = "EXECUTE"
    /\ activeTile /= 0
    /\ tilePower[activeTile] = "ON"
    /\ result' = Infer[activeTile, query]
    /\ state' = "POWERDOWN"
    /\ cycleCounter' = cycleCounter + C_EXECUTE
    /\ history' = AppendBounded(history, "EXECUTE")
    /\ UNCHANGED <<activeTile, query, errorCode, tilePower>>

\* Stage 6.  Power down.  Return to IDLE.
PowerDown ==
    /\ state = "POWERDOWN"
    /\ activeTile /= 0
    /\ tilePower' = AllOff
    /\ activeTile' = 0
    /\ state' = "IDLE"
    /\ cycleCounter' = cycleCounter + C_POWERDOWN
    /\ history' = AppendBounded(history, "POWERDOWN")
    /\ UNCHANGED <<query, result, errorCode>>

\* Safety net.  Not part of the productive path; excluded from fairness.
\* Under the declared budget this action cannot fire on a conforming
\* implementation.  It exists to define the failure semantics.
TimeoutError ==
    /\ state \in {"HARVEST", "TRIAGE", "SCHEDULE", "EXECUTE", "POWERDOWN"}
    /\ cycleCounter >= MaxCycles
    /\ state' = "IDLE"
    /\ activeTile' = 0
    /\ tilePower' = AllOff
    /\ errorCode' = "0x-TIMEOUT"
    /\ cycleCounter' = 0
    /\ history' = AppendBounded(history, "TIMEOUT")
    /\ UNCHANGED <<query, result>>

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Next-state relation
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Next ==
    \/ HarvestIntent
    \/ FISTriage
    \/ FSMSchedule
    \/ TileActivation
    \/ Execute
    \/ PowerDown
    \/ TimeoutError

\* Weak fairness on the productive path only.
Fairness ==
    /\ WF_vars(HarvestIntent)
    /\ WF_vars(FISTriage)
    /\ WF_vars(FSMSchedule)
    /\ WF_vars(TileActivation)
    /\ WF_vars(Execute)
    /\ WF_vars(PowerDown)

Spec == Init /\ [][Next]_vars /\ Fairness

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants (SHALL) — state predicates
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

\* Safety: an executing tile is powered; a zero selection means
\* nothing is powered; a timeout leaves nothing powered.
SafetyInvariant ==
    /\ state = "EXECUTE" => tilePower[activeTile] = "ON"
    /\ activeTile = 0   => tilePower = AllOff
    /\ errorCode = "0x-TIMEOUT" => tilePower = AllOff

\* Timing: the cycle counter never exceeds the budget.
TimingInvariant ==
    cycleCounter <= MaxCycles

\* Isolation: at most one tile is powered at any time.
IsolationInvariant ==
    Cardinality({t \in Tiles : tilePower[t] = "ON"}) <= 1

\* Audit: history stays within the declared bound.
AuditInvariant ==
    Len(history) <= MaxHistory

\* Idle: returning to IDLE clears the tile selection.
IdleInvariant ==
    state = "IDLE" => activeTile = 0

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Liveness (SHALL under the declared fairness)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Termination ==
    [](state /= "IDLE" => <>(state = "IDLE"))

============================================================================
```

File 2 — STT1024_MC.tla (model-checking harness)

```tla
------------------------- MODULE STT1024_MC -------------------------
(***********************************************************************)
(* Model-checking harness for ST-T1024.                                *)
(*                                                                     *)
(* Binds the standard's CONSTANTS to a finite, toy instantiation so    *)
(* that TLC can exhaustively check the scheduler's invariants.         *)
(*                                                                     *)
(* NOT part of the standard.  A conforming implementation binds the    *)
(* same CONSTANTS to real functions.                                   *)
(***********************************************************************)

EXTENDS Integers, Sequences, FiniteSets, TLC

ToyTiles  == {1, 2, 3}
ToyInputs == {"alpha", "beta", "gamma", "delta"}

ToyTriage ==
    [q \in ToyInputs |->
        CASE q = "alpha" -> 1
          [] q = "beta"  -> 2
          [] q = "gamma" -> 0        \* deliberate ambiguity
          [] OTHER      -> 3]

ToyInfer ==
    [t \in ToyTiles, q \in ToyInputs |->
        "out_" \o ToString(t) \o "_" \o q]

MC == INSTANCE STT1024 WITH
    Tiles       <- ToyTiles,
    Inputs      <- ToyInputs,
    TriageFn    <- ToyTriage,
    Infer       <- ToyInfer,
    MaxCycles   <- 400,
    MaxQueryLen <- 256,
    MaxHistory  <- 8

============================================================================
```

File 3 — STT1024.cfg

```
SPECIFICATION MC!Spec

INVARIANTS
    MC!TypeOK
    MC!SafetyInvariant
    MC!TimingInvariant
    MC!IsolationInvariant
    MC!AuditInvariant
    MC!IdleInvariant

PROPERTIES
    MC!Termination
