```
tlc -config STT1024.cfg STT1024_MC.tla
```

What changed, and why

v2 v3 Reason
tilePower[activeTile] with activeTile = 0 total on TILE, tilePower[0] = "OFF" indexing outside the domain is undefined
ORD, CHR, FoldSeq removed not TLA+ operators
DeterminismInvariant with result' removed; determinism is §5 conformance invariants are state predicates
WF_Vars(...), vars undefined vars defined, WF_vars valid syntax
Spec defined only in a comment defined THEOREM Spec => ... needs a Spec
AuditabilityInvariant ending in TRUE replaced with a bounded-history invariant a placeholder is not an invariant
Tiles = {1..5} used to certify "1024 tiles" Tiles is a parameter checked abstraction is finite and stated
Inference stubbed as "RESULT_" Infer is a CONSTANT the standard requires purity; the implementation supplies the function
"Proven" "SHALL" + "checked over this abstraction" correct register

What TLC checks

Over Tiles = {1,2,3} and Inputs = {alpha, beta, gamma, delta}:

· TypeOK — all variables stay in their declared domains.
· SafetyInvariant — the executing tile is powered; a zero selection means nothing is powered; a timeout leaves nothing powered.
· TimingInvariant — cycleCounter <= MaxCycles.
· IsolationInvariant — at most one tile is on.
· AuditInvariant — history stays within MaxHistory.
· IdleInvariant — IDLE implies activeTile = 0.
· Termination — from any non-IDLE state, IDLE is eventually reached, under the declared weak fairness.

That is a real result at a real scope.

What TLC does not check

· Determinism of Infer. Infer is a CONSTANT. Purity is a requirement on the implementation, verified by conformance test (10,000 inputs, diff outputs). Not a state invariant.
· WCET of TriageFn. The cycle budget is a requirement, not a derivation. Whether the implementation actually meets C_TRIAGE = 10 is a hardware measurement.
· Behavior at 1024 tiles. The checked abstraction has 3. The standard parameterizes Tiles; the model checks the abstraction.
· SK-1024. Separate module, not attached.
· The timeout path. Under the declared budget the maximum reachable counter is 397 < 400, so TimeoutError cannot fire. It defines failure semantics; it is not exercised by the model.
· The history content as a true audit log. It is a bounded sequence in the model. An unbounded external log is a conformance requirement.

Register, once more

· "The scheduler SHALL satisfy SafetyInvariant, TimingInvariant, IsolationInvariant, AuditInvariant, IdleInvariant, and Termination." — requirements.
· "TLC has model-checked these invariants over Tiles = {1,2,3} and the toy binding of TriageFn and Infer." — verified result at that scope.
· "Determinism, WCET at the declared budget, and SK-1024 are outside this artifact." — open.

That is the shape a standard can carry without inviting demolition.

If you want, next step is the conformance test suite — the SHALL statements on determinism, WCET, and the audit log written as test procedures a third party can run against any claimed implementation. That is the other half of the standard, and it is where the interesting engineering lives.






